1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,841
GANJEOLGOT CAPE HOPE MAILBOX

2
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:16,099
DESCEND CLUB'S THIRD QUEST IS REVEALED

3
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:19,519
YEONGNAM ALPS' 3-PEAK CHALLENGE

4
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:20,812
We're going to Ulsan.

5
00:00:20,895 --> 00:00:21,938
-Hey!
-My home?

6
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:22,897
It's Tarzzan's home.

7
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:27,110
IT'S WHERE TARZZAN'S HOMETOWN
AND THE YEONGNAM ALPS ARE LOCATED

8
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:32,282
DESCEND CLUB WILL GO
ON AN EXPEDITION TO ULSAN

9
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:35,410
TEXTS FROM DOWOON

10
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:38,913
WHEN WE GO TO ULSAN, ARE WE GOING TO
MEET IN SEOUL AND GO TOGETHER?

11
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:41,541
WE'LL GATHER IN SEOUL
AND GO TOGETHER BY BUS

12
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:43,710
CAN I DRIVE DOWN IN MY OWN CAR?

13
00:00:43,793 --> 00:00:44,753
WHY?

14
00:00:44,836 --> 00:00:47,547
AFTER FILMING, I HAVE A FISHING SHOOT
DURING THE SEOLLAL HOLIDAY

15
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:49,007
OKAY

16
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:51,885
THE DAY THEY LEAVE FOR ULSAN

17
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:55,346
GANGNAM, SEOUL

18
00:00:57,015 --> 00:01:00,018
A BLACK VEHICLE SLOWLY ENTERS

19
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:00,977
He's here.

20
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:02,854
Hello there!

21
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:03,897
Hello.

22
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,274
THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT
GETS OUT SHYLY

23
00:01:06,357 --> 00:01:09,944
Thank you so much for lending us
your car to travel during the holiday.

24
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:11,071
-Lend you my car?
-Yes.

25
00:01:11,154 --> 00:01:12,864
-It's on the way for me anyway.
-Still.

26
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:15,909
MAKING SPACE IN HIS TRUNK
FOR THE OTHER MEMBERS' LUGGAGE

27
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:17,285
-Okay?
-Yeah.

28
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:19,370
-It'll be tight, but they'll go in.
-It'll work.

29
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:21,372
-Yeah.
-The rearview mirror is digital.

30
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:22,290
Right.

31
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:25,085
There's a fridge in here too.

32
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,461
Stop bragging about your car.

33
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:28,046
And it has a digital rearview mirror.

34
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:31,841
Should I lift the car a bit
so you can set the cameras up more easily?

35
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:33,676
I have to go to Wando afterwards.

36
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:35,553
-For fishing.
-For fishing?

37
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:37,722
I'm going to catch yellowtail for my fans.

38
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,891
AN EVENT FOR HIS FANS

39
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:44,145
HE'LL WAIT FOR THE OTHER MEMBERS
IN THE BASEMENT

40
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:48,191
A CUP OF COFFEE TO PREPARE
FOR THE LONG DRIVE AHEAD

41
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:49,692
Gosh.

42
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:52,654
His legacy.

43
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:53,988
Hi, Jung-won.

44
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:56,324
-I heard you're driving.
-Yes.

45
00:01:56,407 --> 00:01:57,784
-You sure you won't be tired?
-Yes.

46
00:01:57,867 --> 00:02:00,411
I mean, we're not even hiking there today.

47
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:03,039
-Hello.
-Hello.

48
00:02:04,165 --> 00:02:06,626
I heard we're going in your car.
What's happening?

49
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:08,044
It'll be much more comfortable.

50
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:09,254
So you're really doing it?

51
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:12,507
IT SEEMS HE TOLD THEM
DURING THEIR SHOOT IN TAEBAEKSAN

52
00:02:13,174 --> 00:02:15,885
By the way, Dowoon,
I saw what you did at your concert.

53
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:17,679
We saw it too.

54
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:20,181
"I'm close with Tarzzan." Was that it?

55
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:21,349
WHAT ARE THEY REFERRING TO?

56
00:02:21,432 --> 00:02:22,851
And he said he touched his beard.

57
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:25,436
A FEW DAYS EARLIER
AT DAY6'S CONCERT IN DAEGU

58
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,689
I'm close with Tarzzan.

59
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:29,190
CHEERING

60
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:31,192
I got to hold Chae-min's hand.

61
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:32,652
EXCLAIMING

62
00:02:32,735 --> 00:02:34,904
I even got to touch
Car, the garden's beard.

63
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:37,157
LAUGHING

64
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:40,702
The fans cheered when he talked about us.

65
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:43,079
But when he talked about Car-the's beard…

66
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:45,039
EMOTIONLESS LAUGHING

67
00:02:45,123 --> 00:02:46,583
Right, I saw that too.

68
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:49,544
It's so embarrassing
that you saw me at my day job.

69
00:02:49,627 --> 00:02:51,337
BLUSHING WITH EMBARRASSMENT

70
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:56,426
One of my relatives really likes hiking.

71
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:59,345
So I asked them
about what the trails are like.

72
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:01,139
They said Hallasan's easy
compared to them.

73
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:02,181
What?

74
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:03,766
Apparently, they're tougher.

75
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:04,684
In this quest?

76
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:05,935
-And they've been there?
-Yes.

77
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:06,853
What?

78
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:09,105
Weren't we told it wasn't tougher?

79
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:10,940
A SHOCKING NEWS THAT WAKES THEM UP

80
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:13,359
They hiked the same three peaks.

81
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:15,445
-They completed all three peaks?
-Yes.

82
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:19,032
When I said we'd hike the three peaks,
they said, "It won't be easy."

83
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:20,533
My car can go off-road.

84
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,785
AND SO, TARZZAN PLANNED

85
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:25,413
DESCEND CLUB'S EXPEDITION TO ULSAN

86
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:27,332
1. LUNCH AT HIS FAVORITE
MILMYEON RESTAURANT

87
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:33,838
Hey, Ulsan is really nice.

88
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:38,051
2. RIDE BICYCLES AT ULSAN GRAND PARK

89
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:41,012
Gosh, this is so nice!

90
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:44,307
3. CHECK IN AT BASE CAMP

91
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:48,019
4. HIKE THE YEONGNAM ALPS

92
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:56,069
5. VISIT PRESIDENT TAR'S FAMILY

93
00:03:56,152 --> 00:04:00,823
A SPECIAL EVENT HAS ALSO BEEN PREPARED

94
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:03,826
DESCEND CLUB DEPARTS
FOR THEIR EXPEDITION TO ULSAN

95
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:05,620
-What a nice car.
-This is my first time.

96
00:04:06,204 --> 00:04:07,914
Defenders are pretty nice.

97
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:10,792
THE MEMBERS LOVE DOWOON'S CAR

98
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:13,711
We'll be able to go comfortably
thanks to Dowoon.

99
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:15,713
LEAVING FOR ULSAN

100
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:18,091
Gosh, it's 371 km.

101
00:04:18,174 --> 00:04:20,635
EXPECTED TO TAKE
ABOUT 4 HOURS AND 30 MINUTES

102
00:04:20,718 --> 00:04:22,679
What are you doing during Seollal?

103
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:24,264
IT BEGINS THE DAY AFTER THE SHOOT

104
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:27,308
I'll be filling in for a radio DJ.

105
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:28,935
So you're working.

106
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:30,353
What about you, Tarzzan?

107
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:33,815
During the holiday?
I think I'll go to work at the studio.

108
00:04:34,399 --> 00:04:37,193
-So this is when you'll visit your mother?
-That's right.

109
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:39,404
Let's each buy something for the family.

110
00:04:39,487 --> 00:04:41,656
-Of course. I gladly will.
-It's Seollal after all.

111
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:43,366
That's what I'm most excited for.

112
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:46,077
Since I was a kid, I've loved
going to a friend's house to eat.

113
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,996
I asked my mom to do
only one thing for me.

114
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:50,415
It was to hide
my embarrassing photos from the past.

115
00:04:50,498 --> 00:04:52,625
-It's fun to have those.
-Have you changed a lot?

116
00:04:52,709 --> 00:04:53,918
I bet you haven't.

117
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:56,879
BABY TARZZAN
LOOKS THE SAME

118
00:04:56,963 --> 00:04:58,965
I really want to see
how Chae-min looked as a kid.

119
00:04:59,048 --> 00:05:00,842
-I bet you have some photos.
-I do.

120
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:02,719
This is how I looked as a kid.

121
00:05:02,802 --> 00:05:04,470
-You look the same.
-He does.

122
00:05:04,554 --> 00:05:06,472
BABY CHAE-MIN
BRIGHT-EYED

123
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:08,641
-You look a bit like Yi-jin.
-What?

124
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:11,311
<i>Yi-jin's the kid who appeared</i>
<i>on my YouTube channel.</i>

125
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:13,313
<i>You kind of look like him.</i>

126
00:05:13,938 --> 00:05:17,233
I bet Dowoon was a super baby
when he was little.

127
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:19,068
-What's a "super baby"?
-What's that?

128
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:20,236
You know. Super babies.

129
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,739
They're babies
who just look absolutely adorable.

130
00:05:22,822 --> 00:05:24,282
There are types of kids like Dowoon.

131
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:27,076
They're babies
who are always smiling in pictures.

132
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,369
And they're chuckling.

133
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:29,329
BABY DOWOON
CHUCKLING

134
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:32,623
I bet he was one of those babies
with big smiles in every photo.

135
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:34,709
I want to see your childhood photo.

136
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:36,210
-Me as a kid?
-Yes.

137
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:37,920
People loved me. I was so cute.

138
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:40,006
BABY CAR-THE?
CUTE…

139
00:05:40,089 --> 00:05:42,508
Do kids still get milk
at school these days?

140
00:05:42,592 --> 00:05:44,635
-You got chocolate milk if you paid more.
-Right.

141
00:05:44,719 --> 00:05:47,555
-Did you guys do the milk delivery too?
-Milk duty? Yes.

142
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:49,098
THEY ALL HAVE SHARED EXPERIENCES

143
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:50,808
You didn't have kerosene heaters, right?

144
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:53,061
-We had them.
-I'm sure you did.

145
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:56,272
KEROSENE HEATERS WERE USED
WHEN CAR-THE AND DOWOON WERE STUDENTS

146
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:57,315
-You had those?
-Yeah.

147
00:05:57,398 --> 00:05:58,816
Did you put your lunchboxes on it?

148
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,734
No lunchboxes.

149
00:05:59,817 --> 00:06:01,360
TREATING HIM LIKE AN OLD-TIMER

150
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:03,029
We had kerosene duty though.

151
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:04,322
We had those things.

152
00:06:04,405 --> 00:06:05,990
For chalkboard eraser dust…

153
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:06,908
The cleaner?

154
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:08,701
YOUNGER KIDS USED
ELECTRIC ERASER CLEANERS

155
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:10,828
We'd make it look like smoke
and go, "Fire!"

156
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,455
THEY PLAYED WITH THE ERASERS A LOT

157
00:06:12,538 --> 00:06:15,416
THE ULTIMATE LITTLE BOY, TARZZAN

158
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,961
SEOUL
ULSAN

159
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,630
GOING SMOOTHLY IN DOWOON'S CAR

160
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:23,299
HE'S BEEN DRIVING
FOR 3 AND A HALF HOURS NOW

161
00:06:23,382 --> 00:06:25,676
-Do you want to switch? Want me to drive?
-What?

162
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:27,345
There's about an hour left.

163
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:28,513
No, I'm good.

164
00:06:29,347 --> 00:06:30,723
Feel free to tell me.

165
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:32,558
I say it if I'm tired.

166
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:34,435
-I just say it.
-All right.

167
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:38,606
DRIVING IS MORE SUITED
FOR THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT THAN HIKING

168
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:41,317
I wonder why they picked
hiking of all things.

169
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,152
Do a lot of people go hiking these days?

170
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:45,613
Well, a lot of people I know around my age

171
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:48,116
go hiking, especially among guys.

172
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:52,411
The popularity of hiking
might've swayed them to make this show.

173
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:55,289
But once this show premieres,

174
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:57,959
what if the number of hikers decreases?

175
00:06:58,042 --> 00:07:00,044
VIEWERS: "GOSH, I SHOULDN'T GO HIKING"

176
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:02,296
That's my ultimate goal.

177
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,758
Through this show,
I want to reduce the number of hikers.

178
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:07,844
This is what I'm worried about.

179
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:10,680
They might think,
"That looks so tough," and that's it.

180
00:07:11,305 --> 00:07:13,474
What if it just ends with us suffering?

181
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:15,184
"I feel bad for them," and that's it?

182
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,019
Or they say,
"They're going through a lot."

183
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:18,688
IN THE MEANTIME, THE CAR KEEPS GOING

184
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:21,941
THEY ARRIVE IN DOWNTOWN ULSAN

185
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:23,693
Gosh.

186
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:26,487
I can feel it, Tarzzan.

187
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:30,116
I can feel that Ulsan is welcoming us.

188
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:32,410
Or is it turning us away with this wind?

189
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:34,370
Of course, it's welcoming us.

190
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:36,247
PRESIDENT TAR IS EXCITED TO BE BACK HOME

191
00:07:36,330 --> 00:07:38,291
It must be nice to be back home, Tarzzan.

192
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:39,500
It's good to be home.

193
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:43,671
It is. And I'm at a loss for words.
It feels so…

194
00:07:43,754 --> 00:07:46,632
That Ferris wheel is a landmark here.

195
00:07:46,716 --> 00:07:49,427
And that's the department store.

196
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:50,761
This must be downtown.

197
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:53,639
IN HIS HOMETOWN,
HE NATURALLY BECOMES AN ULSAN DOCENT

198
00:07:54,223 --> 00:07:55,808
That's my elementary school.

199
00:07:57,894 --> 00:07:59,979
One of our producers
graduated from here too

200
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:01,939
GIGGLING YOUNG TARZZAN

201
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:04,108
Then, Jung-won,

202
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:06,694
how about we have the <i>milmyeon</i> noodles

203
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:09,030
and then go for a walk
in Ulsan Grand Park?

204
00:08:09,113 --> 00:08:10,072
Sounds good.

205
00:08:11,365 --> 00:08:14,952
DESCEND CLUB HEADS
TO THE MILMYEON RESTAURANT

206
00:08:15,036 --> 00:08:17,121
This is the place. We're here.

207
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,415
-This is it?
-Look at the sign.

208
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,501
-It's the real deal.
-It's just like the others.

209
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:25,046
THEY CAN TELL BY THE FADED SIGN
THAT IT'S A GOOD RESTAURANT

210
00:08:25,129 --> 00:08:27,256
Doesn't it already
smell like a good restaurant?

211
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:29,884
A FAVORITE RESTAURANT OF TARZZAN'S
FILLED WITH FOND MEMORIES

212
00:08:29,967 --> 00:08:32,345
MILMYEON

213
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:33,888
<i>Can we take over this place?</i>

214
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:35,723
<i>Let's take this place for ourselves.</i>

215
00:08:35,806 --> 00:08:37,225
<i>This is amazing.</i>

216
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:41,979
MANDU

217
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,984
THE FIRST MEAL IN ULSAN
IS MILMYEON AND MANDU

218
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:48,486
Can we go in?

219
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:49,737
It's this way.

220
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,113
Can we take over this place?

221
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:52,907
STARTS TALKING IN DIALECT UPON GETTING OUT

222
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,659
-Are you ready?
-Sir, can we take it over?

223
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:57,119
-We traveled 400 km for this.
-It's hot.

224
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:59,455
VERY EXCITED FOR FIRST MEAL
AFTER TRAVELING 400 KM

225
00:09:00,581 --> 00:09:03,292
Hey, let me try a bowl of <i>milmyeon.</i>

226
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:04,418
Just one whole bowl.

227
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:05,836
Let's all get chilled broth ones.

228
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:09,215
-Four bowls of <i>mul-milmyeon</i>…
-And two dishes of <i>mandu.</i>

229
00:09:09,298 --> 00:09:10,132
Two orders of <i>mandu?</i>

230
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:14,095
Hey, the owner even remembers
the last day you came.

231
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:15,012
Really?

232
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:17,390
Did you come here
with your mom on January 30?

233
00:09:17,473 --> 00:09:19,475
-I come here every time I visit Ulsan.
-Really?

234
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,894
TARZZAN IS A TRUE REGULAR HERE

235
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:25,606
I've been coming here
since I was three or four years old.

236
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:28,943
This place serves
kid-size portions of noodles.

237
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:32,238
I used to eat the noodles
with a plastic fork as a kid.

238
00:09:33,864 --> 00:09:36,576
The broth smells like
really good <i>seolleongtang.</i>

239
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:37,493
SNIFFING

240
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:38,578
You're right.

241
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:41,872
THEY TRY SOME WARM BROTH
BEFORE THE FOOD COMES OUT

242
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:44,542
Car-the, how do you feel about the broth?

243
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:46,419
First off, well…

244
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:48,546
TRYING TO TALK IN DIALECT AGAIN

245
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:50,089
It's hot.

246
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:53,175
And the spirit
of Gyeongsang people, you know.

247
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:55,469
It's full of that spirit.

248
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,805
The one without cucumbers is his.

249
00:09:57,888 --> 00:09:59,098
We came from Seoul for this.

250
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:00,850
MILMYEON FILLED WITH GYEONGSANG SPIRIT

251
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:04,562
The broth is pretty clear.

252
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:07,607
-Let me check Ulsan's vibes with this.
-Okay.

253
00:10:08,357 --> 00:10:09,609
This is the first impression.

254
00:10:11,193 --> 00:10:13,070
Gosh, this is giving me pressure.

255
00:10:13,821 --> 00:10:15,448
<i>Everyone's liked it so far.</i>

256
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:29,629
It sure is good.

257
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:31,839
Just from the broth, you know it's good.

258
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,429
So you've brought a lot of friends here?

259
00:10:38,512 --> 00:10:39,347
Yeah.

260
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:42,266
Mandu.

261
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:44,644
-Excuse me.
-Thank you.

262
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:45,936
This place is good.

263
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:58,366
A NOSTALGIC TASTE

264
00:11:01,952 --> 00:11:05,790
CHEWY NOODLES THAT ARE ADDICTIVE

265
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:10,503
AND A SPICY AND SWEET BROTH

266
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,630
This is the best.

267
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,256
FEELING VERY PROUD

268
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,883
This place is really good.

269
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,552
TODAY'S GUIDE FEELS REWARDED

270
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:21,222
EXCLAIMING IN SATISFACTION

271
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:29,855
It sure is good.

272
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,109
CAREFULLY TASTES THE MANDU AGAIN

273
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:35,736
I think they make their <i>mandu</i> fresh here.

274
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,779
The <i>mandu</i> is good.

275
00:11:36,862 --> 00:11:38,072
He's a <i>mandu</i> expert.

276
00:11:38,155 --> 00:11:39,740
I don't think they're store-bought.

277
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:41,867
FAVORITE FOOD
MANDU

278
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:43,744
Ma'am, you make the <i>mandu</i> yourself, right?

279
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:45,079
Yes, they're made by hand.

280
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:46,205
I knew it.

281
00:11:46,288 --> 00:11:48,040
I'm fat for a reason.

282
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,210
I didn't gain weight for nothing.

283
00:11:51,293 --> 00:11:52,420
LIKE A HUNGRY UNIT LEADER

284
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:55,005
POKING AROUND

285
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,632
-You can't eat that.
-Is that edible?

286
00:11:57,883 --> 00:11:58,717
No.

287
00:11:58,801 --> 00:12:00,302
-That's not a <i>mandu</i> wrapper.
-No.

288
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:01,846
I was checking the ripped cloth.

289
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:04,682
-I thought he was going to eat it.
-I thought you tried to eat it.

290
00:12:04,765 --> 00:12:06,642
HE LOVES EATING FOOD, NOT CLOTH

291
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:08,811
Car, the garden's song,

292
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:11,355
"My Whole World."
I listen to it every day.

293
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:12,690
Hey, Car-the.

294
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:15,443
Ma'am, tell him.
What do you listen to every day?

295
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:17,153
"My Whole World."

296
00:12:17,236 --> 00:12:23,451
YOU'VE BECOME MY WHOLE WORLD, MA'AM

297
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:26,537
YOU'VE LET ME TASTE MILMYEON
I'VE NEVER HAD BEFORE

298
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,038
She said so shyly,

299
00:12:28,122 --> 00:12:29,957
"I listen to his song every day."

300
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:33,043
Ma'am, do you know DAY6 by any chance?

301
00:12:33,127 --> 00:12:34,211
He's the drummer.

302
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:38,174
Hey, Ulsan is really nice.

303
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:40,468
Ma'am, I'm all done.

304
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,512
CELEBRATING HIS FINISHED BOWL

305
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:47,224
Gosh, what's that?

306
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:49,435
THEY'RE SURPRISED AT SOMETHING

307
00:12:52,396 --> 00:12:54,773
-Did you put your trail snacks in there?
-Yeah.

308
00:12:55,524 --> 00:12:56,567
How did you know?

309
00:12:57,359 --> 00:12:59,904
If I put it in here,
I won't have to wear a backpack.

310
00:12:59,987 --> 00:13:02,948
EASIER TO TAKE OUT AND EAT TOO

311
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:06,452
NEXT DESTINATION
MOVING TO ULSAN GRAND PARK

312
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:09,288
HEARING A CALL AS SOON AS THEY GET IN

313
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:10,539
Who are you suddenly calling?

314
00:13:10,623 --> 00:13:11,874
It's just that…

315
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:13,501
I have a friend who lives here.

316
00:13:14,502 --> 00:13:15,628
Tell him to come out.

317
00:13:16,212 --> 00:13:17,379
Tell him to come to the park.

318
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:18,797
LET'S MEET DOWOON'S FRIEND

319
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:20,674
Hey, are you in Ulsan?

320
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:22,384
<i>Yeah, I am.</i>

321
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:25,095
Hey, I'm at Children's Grand Park…

322
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:27,473
No, I mean Ulsan Grand Park.

323
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:29,850
I'm at the park. Want to come?

324
00:13:30,392 --> 00:13:32,102
<i>I'm working the night shift today.</i>

325
00:13:33,521 --> 00:13:35,314
<i>-When are you here until?</i>
-The 13th.

326
00:13:35,397 --> 00:13:36,607
Want to go hiking?

327
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,151
<i>You're staying in Ulsan until the 13th?</i>

328
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:41,195
Do you know the Young Alps in Ulsan?

329
00:13:41,278 --> 00:13:42,780
YOUNG ALPS?

330
00:13:42,863 --> 00:13:44,532
LAUGHING

331
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:45,908
<i>What? Young…</i>

332
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:47,326
I mean the Yeongnam Alps.

333
00:13:47,409 --> 00:13:51,580
"Young Alps"!

334
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,499
THE "YOUNG ALPS" HIKER IS EMBARRASSED

335
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:54,833
<i>Of course, I know.</i>

336
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:56,001
Want to go hiking?

337
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:58,671
<i>Call me again after you finish hiking.</i>

338
00:13:58,754 --> 00:13:59,713
Bye.

339
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,090
DISCUSSION IS OVER

340
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:02,633
"Young Alps"?

341
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:05,678
That was so…

342
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:07,846
MOCKING STARTS AS SOON AS HE HANGS UP

343
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:12,184
For a moment, I thought that
was what people called them here.

344
00:14:12,268 --> 00:14:15,145
You can rent tandem bicycles at the park.

345
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:17,523
Nice. Let's take over the place.

346
00:14:18,857 --> 00:14:21,402
THEY ARRIVE AT ULSAN GRAND PARK

347
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:24,154
It's been ages since I've been here.

348
00:14:26,782 --> 00:14:28,576
LITTLE TARZZAN USED TO PLAY HERE

349
00:14:28,659 --> 00:14:33,372
THE LARGEST URBAN PARK IN KOREA

350
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:41,171
Sir, we'd like to rent
two tandem bicycles.

351
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:45,551
DESCEND CLUB WILL BECOME CLOSER
WITH THE TANDEM BICYCLES

352
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:46,760
So how do we pair up?

353
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:48,846
Someone light should get on behind me.

354
00:14:48,929 --> 00:14:50,472
-Should I ride with him?
-Sure.

355
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:53,434
WEIGHTS ARE BALANCED OUT
ON CAR-THE & TARZZAN'S BIKE

356
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:56,103
-Dowoon, I'll take the front.
-Okay.

357
00:14:56,186 --> 00:14:58,355
FRONT AND REAR ARE SETTLED
ON CHAE-MIN & DOWOON'S BIKE

358
00:14:59,565 --> 00:15:02,860
FOR TODAY, THEY'RE IN PAIRS
TO RIDE BICYCLES, NOT HIKE

359
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:09,950
I love this. The air is so nice.

360
00:15:10,534 --> 00:15:11,619
The air is nice.

361
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:17,082
TAKING IN ALL THE FRESH AIR

362
00:15:23,547 --> 00:15:26,842
RIDING TOGETHER
AND AS MUCH AS THEY PLEASE

363
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:29,261
They designed this park really well.

364
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:31,555
I know. It's really big.

365
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:34,934
It's like Central Park in Ulsan.

366
00:15:35,684 --> 00:15:38,646
IT'S MUCH NICER AT THE PARK
SINCE THEY'RE TOGETHER

367
00:15:39,313 --> 00:15:40,856
This is a really good date spot.

368
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:43,943
It's starting to feel like
a reality dating show.

369
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,361
How is it, Dowoon?

370
00:15:46,111 --> 00:15:47,738
Oh, my gosh!

371
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:51,367
DO-SOON DOESN'T SEEM TO MIND
CHAE-CHEOL'S BICYCLE FLIRTING

372
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:53,994
WHEREAS JUNG-WON APPEARS
AS IF HE WANTS TO GO HOME

373
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:55,412
Later on at night…

374
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:56,538
Want to go hiking?

375
00:15:57,456 --> 00:15:58,415
I don't think so.

376
00:15:58,499 --> 00:15:59,625
PRETENDING NOT TO HEAR

377
00:15:59,708 --> 00:16:01,460
That would get me rejected right away.

378
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:05,130
A BICYCLE DATE IN THE MOUNTAINS
BECOMES MORE AND MORE UNCERTAIN

379
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:07,883
I liked it. Thanks to Tarzzan…

380
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:11,637
He created fond memories for us.

381
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,180
IT MEANS HE LIKED THE BIKE RIDE

382
00:16:13,263 --> 00:16:16,100
I don't really try to go to parks often.

383
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:17,977
But every time I go, it's nice.

384
00:16:18,727 --> 00:16:20,187
So, it was nice when we went.

385
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:25,859
There's a famous slide here
that I used to play on as a kid.

386
00:16:25,943 --> 00:16:27,069
Let's go there.

387
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:29,613
Sure, since we're here.

388
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:32,449
THEY GO LOOK FOR THE SLIDE
LITTLE TARZZAN PLAYED ON

389
00:16:33,033 --> 00:16:35,577
Geez… It's uphill.

390
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:39,206
UPHILL ALL OF A SUDDEN

391
00:16:39,289 --> 00:16:43,669
TANDEM BICYCLES AT ULSAN GRAND PARK
CAN BE RIDDEN UPHILL BUT NOT DOWNHILL

392
00:16:45,421 --> 00:16:46,463
What is this?

393
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:47,715
QUICKLY GETS STEEPER

394
00:16:47,798 --> 00:16:49,758
Hey, we need to think about this.

395
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:52,011
We're using up our energy!

396
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,971
-I think we made the wrong choice.
-Exactly.

397
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:56,598
-My legs are getting tired.
-We should've ridden that carriage!

398
00:16:56,682 --> 00:16:58,851
We might not be able to hike tomorrow.

399
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:01,311
1ST LINEUP OF THE ULSAN GRAND PARK
MOUNTAIN BIKE RACE

400
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:03,313
Tarzzan, this isn't right.

401
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:04,690
Hey, stop. Let's turn back.

402
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:05,983
LEAD: CHAE-MIN & DOWOON

403
00:17:06,066 --> 00:17:09,570
TAIL: CAR, THE GARDEN & TARZZAN

404
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:10,988
Hey, why…

405
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:12,990
Why are we doing this right now?

406
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:15,659
NEW SHOW IS CALLED
RIDE A MOUNTAIN BIKE!

407
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:17,036
Why are we doing this?

408
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:19,788
There's something called
"The Wishing Stone" on our right.

409
00:17:20,831 --> 00:17:22,124
Don't explain, damn it!

410
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:23,751
What on earth?

411
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:26,962
They're mocking us, aren't they?

412
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:30,924
THEY DON'T HAVE THE ENERGY TO ANSWER

413
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:33,260
That over there
is why I brought you guys here.

414
00:17:33,343 --> 00:17:34,803
-To come here?
-Yes.

415
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:35,929
-Okay.
-What is this place?

416
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:38,098
It's filled
with my childhood memories here.

417
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:39,725
A NOSTALGIC LONG SLIDE

418
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:41,060
It's so long.

419
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:43,103
THE SLIDE IS VERY LONG

420
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:46,315
AND THE BOTTOM LOOKS QUITE PAINFUL

421
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:49,526
Gosh, this slide is really long.

422
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:50,486
Wait.

423
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:52,237
We have to climb.

424
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:55,449
It's like Seoraksan.

425
00:17:55,532 --> 00:17:56,366
What?

426
00:17:57,451 --> 00:17:58,994
You packed your trail food earlier.

427
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:00,370
STOMACH PACKED WITH MILMYEON

428
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,289
Let's take a break up there.

429
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:05,125
DESCEND CLUB RULES
BREAKS: LESS THAN 5 MINUTES

430
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:07,669
A PREVIEW OF THE INSIDE OF THE SLIDE

431
00:18:13,675 --> 00:18:16,386
2ND LINEUP OF THE ULSAN GRAND PARK HIKE
LEAD: CAR, THE GARDEN

432
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:19,264
THEY FIND IT HILARIOUS
TO SEE HIM SLIDE DOWN

433
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:24,812
CAR, THE GARDEN

434
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:26,814
SCREAMING

435
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:28,732
It's really loud.

436
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:31,401
A SILENT SCREAM

437
00:18:32,236 --> 00:18:33,904
My butt hurts so fucking much!

438
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:35,864
My butt!

439
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:38,784
PAIN ON THE BACKSIDE AS EXPECTED

440
00:18:38,867 --> 00:18:43,455
AFTER ENJOYING THE NOSTALGIC PLAYGROUND

441
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:44,957
Hey, Dowoon.

442
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:48,043
Thank you for coming, everyone.

443
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:49,336
THEY LEAVE FOR BASE CAMP

444
00:18:50,003 --> 00:18:51,130
I feel a bit bad.

445
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:54,174
Why would you? It was fun. Seriously.

446
00:18:54,758 --> 00:18:56,135
-Don't be sorry.
-Right.

447
00:18:56,218 --> 00:18:57,970
"Alps Guesthouse."

448
00:18:58,053 --> 00:18:58,887
Is that the name?

449
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:00,430
BASE CAMP IS NEAR THE YEONGNAM ALPS

450
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:02,558
"Baenae Golyeongnam Alps Guesthouse."

451
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:03,976
Still, I bet it'll be nice.

452
00:19:04,059 --> 00:19:06,937
They always pick the best accommodations.

453
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:08,188
This is it. "Yeongnam Alps."

454
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:11,942
BAENAEGOL YEONGNAM ALPS

455
00:19:12,025 --> 00:19:16,029
TODAY'S ACCOMMODATIONS
ARE SURROUNDED BY THE YEONGNAM ALPS

456
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:20,576
YEONGNAM ALPS

457
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:24,788
THE PERFECT BASE CAMP FOR THE DESCEND CLUB

458
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:33,422
THE MEMBERS ARE ASSIGNED
TO THE BIGGEST ONE

459
00:19:34,047 --> 00:19:36,133
-Thank you, Dowoon.
-Thank you so much.

460
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:37,259
My pleasure.

461
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:39,845
GRUNTS

462
00:19:39,928 --> 00:19:42,514
TAKING THEIR LUGGAGE IN

463
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:45,225
Geez, there are stairs everywhere.

464
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:56,111
CAR, THE GARDEN ENTERS FIRST

465
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:58,822
QUICKLY LOOKING AROUND

466
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:00,991
It really feels like a guesthouse here.

467
00:20:01,074 --> 00:20:03,368
IT IS A GUESTHOUSE

468
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:06,079
This place is like… You know?

469
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:07,915
Where Cho Seung-woo, Ji Jin-hee stayed…

470
00:20:07,998 --> 00:20:09,499
-With Hwang Jung-min.
-Yeah.

471
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:11,752
The vibe here reminds you of them.

472
00:20:11,835 --> 00:20:14,254
A SOFA THAT CATCHES YOUR EYE

473
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:22,554
THE MINISTER OF TRANSPORT
IS AWAY IN DREAMLAND

474
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:25,682
I should take a nap too.

475
00:20:29,228 --> 00:20:30,687
Why is he twitching his shoulder?

476
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:32,439
He's asleep.

477
00:20:32,522 --> 00:20:33,649
Is that a sleep habit?

478
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:35,734
He keeps doing it.

479
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,653
Maybe he's playing the drums?

480
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:40,906
HE CAN'T HELP BUT RECORD IT

481
00:20:40,989 --> 00:20:42,324
TARZZAN'S PHONE CAMERA

482
00:20:42,407 --> 00:20:45,410
TYPICAL SLEEP HABIT OF DRUMMERS

483
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:53,669
SNORING

484
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:56,797
WITHIN 3 MINUTES,
THEY HEAR FAMILIAR SNORING

485
00:20:57,589 --> 00:21:00,050
OFF AGAIN TO CHECK

486
00:21:03,971 --> 00:21:08,558
TARZZAN'S PHONE CAMERA

487
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:11,687
SNORE, THE GARDEN

488
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:19,319
AND SO, DESCEND CLUB HAS A PEACEFUL TIME

489
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:21,321
IN THE MEANTIME

490
00:21:21,905 --> 00:21:25,867
THEY HAD A SMALL WISH

491
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:27,577
I want to film <i>Earth Arcade.</i>

492
00:21:28,245 --> 00:21:29,830
I'm so envious of them.

493
00:21:30,455 --> 00:21:31,873
I'm so jealous.

494
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:35,043
Are we playing
Guess the Celebrities today?

495
00:21:35,752 --> 00:21:37,337
I think I'd be so good at it.

496
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:38,505
OBSESSED WITH EARTH ARCADE

497
00:21:38,588 --> 00:21:41,425
Let's decide by playing
Guess the Celebrities.

498
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:43,760
I want to play
Guess the Celebrities so bad.

499
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:46,638
SINCE HE WANTED TO PLAY IT SO MUCH

500
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:51,560
THE PRODUCTION CREW
IS PREPARING A SIMPLE ACTIVITY

501
00:21:51,643 --> 00:21:54,479
On your way out,
please take your backpacks with you.

502
00:21:54,563 --> 00:21:56,481
-Okay.
-Just your backpacks.

503
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:58,233
You mean our hiking backpacks?

504
00:21:58,317 --> 00:21:59,192
Yes.

505
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:02,321
WITHOUT KNOWING WHY,
THEY EACH TAKE THEIR BACKPACKS

506
00:22:02,404 --> 00:22:03,739
AND MOVE TO THE ACTIVITY AREA

507
00:22:03,822 --> 00:22:06,616
You can finally play
the Guess the Celebrities game you wanted.

508
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:08,076
I'm really good at it.

509
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:10,662
Even if you know,

510
00:22:10,746 --> 00:22:12,581
you get flustered
when they're suddenly shown.

511
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:13,749
You think so?

512
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:14,791
A FAMILIAR SCENE ON TV

513
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:15,834
You end up like that.

514
00:22:15,917 --> 00:22:17,544
You're right.

515
00:22:17,627 --> 00:22:18,754
There it is.

516
00:22:19,671 --> 00:22:21,048
Gosh, it's scary.

517
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:23,216
They made it look so serious.

518
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:26,553
-It looks serious.
-It's kind of set up like <i>Earth Arcade.</i>

519
00:22:26,636 --> 00:22:27,471
ACTIVITY AREA

520
00:22:27,554 --> 00:22:28,972
There are a lot of cameras.

521
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:30,807
THE SET LAYOUT THEY'VE SEEN A LOT ON TV

522
00:22:30,891 --> 00:22:32,267
We're finally doing <i>Earth Arcade.</i>

523
00:22:33,852 --> 00:22:34,978
Come on in.

524
00:22:35,062 --> 00:22:36,605
Hey, it's <i>Earth Arcade!</i>

525
00:22:37,147 --> 00:22:40,192
Come in and have a seat first.

526
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:41,568
It's time for activities.

527
00:22:43,361 --> 00:22:45,530
-Dowoon. Are you okay?
-Yes? Yes.

528
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:46,948
HE'S STILL HALF ASLEEP

529
00:22:47,699 --> 00:22:50,660
THE FIERY RED PRESIDENT ALSO ENTERS

530
00:22:50,744 --> 00:22:54,206
THEY'VE ALL ENTERED WITH THEIR BACKPACKS

531
00:22:54,289 --> 00:22:56,583
HE PREPARED THE FINGER STICK TOO

532
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:58,460
Gosh, he has that stick too.

533
00:22:59,002 --> 00:23:00,670
THEY'VE ONLY SEEN IT BEFORE ON TV

534
00:23:00,754 --> 00:23:02,339
It finally feels like a variety show.

535
00:23:02,422 --> 00:23:04,382
You guys are in trouble today.

536
00:23:05,383 --> 00:23:06,551
This is so cool.

537
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:08,804
You'll end up saying,
"Please make me go hiking."

538
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:10,180
This is amazing.

539
00:23:10,972 --> 00:23:14,726
THE EARTH ARCADE FAN FINDS EVERYTHING COOL

540
00:23:15,727 --> 00:23:17,521
We're going to do a group mission.

541
00:23:17,604 --> 00:23:18,980
All four of you will team up.

542
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:21,108
We'll play a simple game

543
00:23:21,191 --> 00:23:23,902
to determine whether you succeed or fail.

544
00:23:24,736 --> 00:23:27,030
This is already so nice. Why go hiking?

545
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:30,784
If I were watching this,
I'd think, "This will be fun!"

546
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:33,286
If I were a viewer,

547
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:35,205
I'd already be excited.

548
00:23:35,288 --> 00:23:37,040
I think hiking is more fun,

549
00:23:37,124 --> 00:23:38,834
but you guys wanted to do this so badly.

550
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:40,377
-Let us try.
-We'll give you a taste.

551
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:42,629
-We should at least have a taste.
-Just a taste.

552
00:23:42,712 --> 00:23:44,673
It's like free samples at a supermarket.

553
00:23:44,756 --> 00:23:45,841
It's just a tasting.

554
00:23:45,924 --> 00:23:48,468
How about we bet something small?

555
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:51,721
Nothing related to hiking, right?

556
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:52,889
What do you think it'll be?

557
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:56,268
If we win, would the number of peaks
shrink from three to two?

558
00:23:57,185 --> 00:23:59,604
But what if you fail
and have to hike four peaks?

559
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,314
Should I stop talking?

560
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:07,237
Now, why do you think
we asked you to bring your backpacks?

561
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,947
Wait, are we putting things in them?

562
00:24:09,030 --> 00:24:10,615
More stuff!

563
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:12,284
It's more stuff!

564
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:14,077
Wait, that's a good idea too.

565
00:24:14,161 --> 00:24:15,203
THAT WASN'T IT

566
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:16,496
We didn't think of that.

567
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:19,416
Why backpacks? I have no idea.

568
00:24:20,083 --> 00:24:21,459
Chae-min, show us yours.

569
00:24:22,919 --> 00:24:26,214
You have kilometer badges
that you've worked so hard to earn.

570
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:29,676
If we play with nothing at stake,
it would be no fun.

571
00:24:29,759 --> 00:24:33,513
You guys are about to reach
50 km soon.

572
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:35,140
CURRENT TOTAL DISTANCES

573
00:24:35,223 --> 00:24:37,309
If you reach 50 km,

574
00:24:37,392 --> 00:24:39,102
-we'll give you gold badges.
-Okay.

575
00:24:39,186 --> 00:24:41,646
PRIZE FOR 50 KM: A GOLD BADGE

576
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,440
If you reach 100 km,

577
00:24:43,523 --> 00:24:46,985
we'll give you the right to change
the theme of our show as you like.

578
00:24:47,068 --> 00:24:49,154
IF THEY REACH 100 KM,
THEY CAN CHANGE THE SHOW

579
00:24:49,237 --> 00:24:52,949
You guys are about to reach
50 km soon.

580
00:24:53,033 --> 00:24:56,286
So at this critical juncture,

581
00:24:56,369 --> 00:24:57,746
we'll play a game,

582
00:24:58,830 --> 00:25:01,666
and you'll bet a kilometer per round.

583
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,793
I wondered why
they were suddenly doing this.

584
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:07,255
They saw us
and were starting to get nervous.

585
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:09,049
They thought they were being too generous.

586
00:25:09,132 --> 00:25:10,050
SCARED

587
00:25:10,133 --> 00:25:12,010
No, this is really good for you.

588
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:14,679
For every round, 1 km is on the line.

589
00:25:14,763 --> 00:25:15,972
We can win them too?

590
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:18,141
-Yes, we'll give them to you.
-We'll just win then.

591
00:25:18,225 --> 00:25:21,186
FAIL AND LOSE 1 KM
WIN AND EARN 1 KM

592
00:25:21,269 --> 00:25:22,395
That's if you win.

593
00:25:22,479 --> 00:25:24,940
Then, the show might change right away.

594
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:26,191
INTRIGUED

595
00:25:26,274 --> 00:25:28,068
Do you hate hiking that much?

596
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:30,695
We just need to win 50 rounds.

597
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:32,364
FEELS SO FAR AWAY

598
00:25:32,447 --> 00:25:34,324
HIKING SEEMS EASIER

599
00:25:34,407 --> 00:25:35,784
Just 50 rounds!

600
00:25:35,867 --> 00:25:39,120
If anyone gets something wrong,
let's not blame them too much.

601
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:41,414
Let's not doubt each other.
Be encouraging.

602
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:43,750
We're one team, right?

603
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:47,545
HESITATING

604
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,839
I thought, "He and I are a team?"

605
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:52,717
"But he's so handsome."

606
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:54,052
I mean, his eyes looked so…

607
00:25:54,135 --> 00:25:55,929
Because I've never had anyone

608
00:25:56,012 --> 00:25:58,223
who was this handsome
on the same team as me.

609
00:25:59,599 --> 00:26:01,768
I was like, "Thanks, man."

610
00:26:01,851 --> 00:26:04,020
NO GUESS THE CELEBRITIES
DUE TO PUBLICITY RIGHTS ISSUES

611
00:26:04,104 --> 00:26:05,063
We have something else.

612
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:07,899
Let's start with a simple one.
"The Category Game."

613
00:26:07,983 --> 00:26:10,443
-Okay, "The Category Game."
-I'll explain what it is.

614
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:12,320
-There are many kinds of <i>ramyeon.</i>
-Right.

615
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:14,698
Say a name of <i>ramyeon.</i>
Chae-min first. Go.

616
00:26:14,781 --> 00:26:15,615
Samyang Ramen.

617
00:26:15,699 --> 00:26:16,950
-Snack Ramen.
-Next. Okay.

618
00:26:17,033 --> 00:26:18,159
-Next.
-Shin Ramyun.

619
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:19,661
-Next.
-Nongshim Ramyun.

620
00:26:19,744 --> 00:26:20,704
Next. What?

621
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:22,414
-It's not Nongshim Ramyun?
-Wrong.

622
00:26:22,497 --> 00:26:24,708
-Yeul Ramen.
-But there is Nongshim Ramyeon.

623
00:26:24,791 --> 00:26:26,126
-Really?
-Come on.

624
00:26:26,209 --> 00:26:27,752
-It was released.
-Hey!

625
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:30,088
-I was right then!
-See?

626
00:26:30,171 --> 00:26:33,341
Viewers would be like,
"That <i>ramyeon</i> exists though!"

627
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:35,385
"This is so fun!"

628
00:26:35,468 --> 00:26:37,178
Look at how fun this is.

629
00:26:37,262 --> 00:26:40,515
I feel like I'm losing all my confidence
because of this show.

630
00:26:41,224 --> 00:26:43,143
It's fine, but do we get a practice round?

631
00:26:43,226 --> 00:26:44,102
Should we do that?

632
00:26:44,185 --> 00:26:45,395
-Let's do a practice one.
-Yes.

633
00:26:45,478 --> 00:26:46,896
Okay, let's do it.

634
00:26:46,980 --> 00:26:47,814
PRACTICE ROUND

635
00:26:47,897 --> 00:26:48,732
Chae-min will start.

636
00:26:48,815 --> 00:26:50,275
Gosh, I feel nervous.

637
00:26:51,067 --> 00:26:52,652
What's your favorite hobby, Dowoon?

638
00:26:52,736 --> 00:26:54,195
-Fishing.
-Fishing, right?

639
00:26:54,821 --> 00:26:56,698
So when you go fishing, you catch fish.

640
00:26:56,781 --> 00:26:58,533
Okay, out of fish names,

641
00:26:58,616 --> 00:27:01,286
say a name that ends with "<i>chi</i>" in Korean.

642
00:27:01,369 --> 00:27:02,746
Chae-min first. One, two, three.

643
00:27:02,829 --> 00:27:04,372
<i>-Jagalchi.</i>
<i>-Nalchi.</i>

644
00:27:04,456 --> 00:27:05,749
-"<i>Jagalchi</i>"?
-Yes.

645
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:06,666
Let's check later.

646
00:27:06,750 --> 00:27:07,625
-Next.
<i>-Nalchi.</i>

647
00:27:07,709 --> 00:27:09,127
-Next.
<i>-Chamchi</i> or tuna.

648
00:27:09,210 --> 00:27:10,045
<i>Chamchi.</i>

649
00:27:10,128 --> 00:27:11,504
-Next.
<i>-Myeolchi</i> or anchovy.

650
00:27:11,588 --> 00:27:12,464
Next.

651
00:27:12,547 --> 00:27:14,007
<i>Darangi geonban chamchi.</i>

652
00:27:16,009 --> 00:27:17,385
<i>Darangi geonban chamchi.</i>

653
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:22,057
<i>"Darangi geonban chamchi"?</i>

654
00:27:22,140 --> 00:27:23,933
ON EGGSHELLS

655
00:27:24,017 --> 00:27:25,935
-What else was there? Think.
<i>-Galchi.</i>

656
00:27:26,603 --> 00:27:27,812
I was stuck too.

657
00:27:28,646 --> 00:27:29,814
"Stuck-chi!"

658
00:27:30,482 --> 00:27:31,524
What were you thinking of?

659
00:27:31,608 --> 00:27:32,901
Nothing. I was done.

660
00:27:32,984 --> 00:27:34,569
-Your mind went blank?
-Yes.

661
00:27:34,652 --> 00:27:35,945
-Okay, "<i>chi</i>."
-That was hard.

662
00:27:36,029 --> 00:27:36,863
Let's go.

663
00:27:36,946 --> 00:27:39,074
-Fish names are difficult.
-Yeah.

664
00:27:39,157 --> 00:27:41,910
But how do we win?
How many laps do we need to do?

665
00:27:41,993 --> 00:27:44,954
IF THEY MAKE ONE FULL LAP, THEY WIN

666
00:27:45,038 --> 00:27:47,207
-I think we'll lose them all.
-That can't happen.

667
00:27:47,290 --> 00:27:49,084
They must be doing this to take them all.

668
00:27:49,167 --> 00:27:52,295
-And they'll take us to higher mountains.
-With ridiculous quizzes.

669
00:27:52,379 --> 00:27:53,713
They didn't do this last week.

670
00:27:53,797 --> 00:27:54,839
THEY SEE THE PLANS CLEARLY

671
00:27:54,923 --> 00:27:57,050
-They must be anxious.
-Yeah. Right?

672
00:27:57,717 --> 00:27:59,844
FYI GOLD PRICES
WERE SKYROCKETING ON DATE OF FILMING

673
00:27:59,928 --> 00:28:02,097
We can give you gold if we have to.

674
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:03,973
-So a kilometer is on the line.
-Okay.

675
00:28:04,057 --> 00:28:05,392
Here goes the first round.

676
00:28:05,475 --> 00:28:06,643
FAIL: LOSE 1 KM
WIN: EARN 1 KM

677
00:28:06,726 --> 00:28:07,644
We can do it.

678
00:28:07,727 --> 00:28:08,561
I'm nervous.

679
00:28:09,437 --> 00:28:10,522
I'm so nervous.

680
00:28:11,272 --> 00:28:12,857
We'll start with Chae-min,

681
00:28:12,941 --> 00:28:15,151
go to Dowoon, and end back at Chae-min.

682
00:28:15,860 --> 00:28:19,364
Now, we're in Tarzzan's hometown.
What is it called?

683
00:28:19,447 --> 00:28:21,074
-Ulsan.
-Yes, we're in Ulsan.

684
00:28:21,157 --> 00:28:24,869
Say a word that starts
with "<i>ul</i>" in Korean.

685
00:28:24,953 --> 00:28:26,663
-Chae-min first. One, two, three!
<i>-Ulbo.</i>

686
00:28:26,746 --> 00:28:28,331
-One, two, three!
-Uljin.

687
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:29,666
-One, two, three!
-Ulju County.

688
00:28:29,749 --> 00:28:31,376
-One, two, three!
<i>-Ulleong</i> or nauseous.

689
00:28:31,459 --> 00:28:32,669
One, two, three!

690
00:28:32,752 --> 00:28:34,087
<i>-Ulbin.</i>
-Wrong!

691
00:28:34,170 --> 00:28:35,422
What on earth is that?

692
00:28:35,505 --> 00:28:36,714
-What's "<i>ulbin</i>"?
-"<i>Ulbin</i>"?

693
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:38,258
<i>-Ulbin.</i>
-Wrong!

694
00:28:38,341 --> 00:28:39,717
What on earth is that?

695
00:28:39,801 --> 00:28:41,010
What's "<i>ulbin</i>"?

696
00:28:41,678 --> 00:28:42,929
-What's "<i>ulbin</i>"?
-"<i>Ulbin</i>"?

697
00:28:44,305 --> 00:28:45,306
You can look it up.

698
00:28:45,390 --> 00:28:46,725
-You have to explain.
-First off…

699
00:28:46,808 --> 00:28:48,017
You can do it. What's "<i>ulbin</i>"?

700
00:28:48,101 --> 00:28:49,811
-What's "<i>ulbin</i>"?
-What is it?

701
00:28:49,894 --> 00:28:51,312
"Eating <i>bindae-tteok</i> while crying."

702
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:53,565
"Eating <i>bindae-tteok</i> while crying."

703
00:28:53,648 --> 00:28:54,899
FRUSTRATED TO TEARS

704
00:28:54,983 --> 00:28:57,402
-That's…
-Can you check if it exists?

705
00:28:59,487 --> 00:29:01,030
-There was Ulleungdo Island.
-Right.

706
00:29:01,114 --> 00:29:02,240
RIGHT…

707
00:29:02,323 --> 00:29:04,117
But this spot is tough.

708
00:29:04,951 --> 00:29:06,411
What were you going to say, Car-the?

709
00:29:06,494 --> 00:29:08,580
-Ulleungdo Island.
-Not bad.

710
00:29:08,663 --> 00:29:11,291
I was going to say Ulleungdo Island.
I just told him.

711
00:29:12,041 --> 00:29:15,003
THE SLY BEARDED ONE

712
00:29:15,086 --> 00:29:18,465
Your mind goes blank
because you get nervous.

713
00:29:18,548 --> 00:29:19,841
There was a lot, like "<i>ulkeok</i>."

714
00:29:19,924 --> 00:29:22,010
But I couldn't think of it in the moment.

715
00:29:22,093 --> 00:29:23,219
<i>Ulgeum</i> or turmeric.

716
00:29:24,220 --> 00:29:25,555
<i>Uldae</i> or Adam's apple.

717
00:29:25,638 --> 00:29:26,598
Right.

718
00:29:27,557 --> 00:29:30,143
A lot of them come to mind
after the game ends.

719
00:29:31,186 --> 00:29:32,979
So that was a practice round, right?

720
00:29:33,062 --> 00:29:34,355
Yeah, a practice round.

721
00:29:34,439 --> 00:29:35,815
All right, thank you.

722
00:29:36,399 --> 00:29:37,692
-What?
-Okay, a kilometer each.

723
00:29:38,359 --> 00:29:39,944
TAKES A 1-KM BADGE FROM EVERYONE

724
00:29:40,028 --> 00:29:41,446
Tarzzan, give him one more.

725
00:29:41,529 --> 00:29:42,363
What?

726
00:29:44,908 --> 00:29:47,702
Just like that,
we already lost a kilometer each.

727
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:49,078
We lost a total of 4 km already.

728
00:29:49,162 --> 00:29:51,748
You lost about 30 minutes
of hiking from Seongpanak trail.

729
00:29:53,041 --> 00:29:55,168
Now that you explain it that way…

730
00:29:55,251 --> 00:29:56,544
A SHOCKING NEWS

731
00:29:56,628 --> 00:29:58,171
It's a game where time is stolen.

732
00:29:58,254 --> 00:29:59,339
ABOUT TO CRY

733
00:29:59,422 --> 00:30:01,549
We just lost
a whole section of stairs in time.

734
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:02,801
Right…

735
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:06,012
Now that I think of it that way,
it's so sad.

736
00:30:06,095 --> 00:30:07,305
Right?

737
00:30:07,388 --> 00:30:08,932
Okay, what now then?

738
00:30:09,015 --> 00:30:10,016
Should we stop?

739
00:30:10,099 --> 00:30:11,601
-Yes, let's stop.
-Let's stop.

740
00:30:11,684 --> 00:30:12,852
VERY WISE

741
00:30:12,936 --> 00:30:14,312
In my opinion…

742
00:30:14,813 --> 00:30:16,022
Let's stop here.

743
00:30:16,105 --> 00:30:18,107
-I mean, we got a little taste.
-You did.

744
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:19,150
We're done now.

745
00:30:19,234 --> 00:30:21,820
But shouldn't you play one more round

746
00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:23,488
to recover your losses?

747
00:30:24,155 --> 00:30:25,532
This is how gambling works.

748
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:27,784
-Should we raise the stakes?
-"You should get it back."

749
00:30:27,867 --> 00:30:30,161
THE CRYING BINDAE-TTEOK EATER
IS AGGRESSIVE

750
00:30:30,245 --> 00:30:32,580
A guy like you will end up losing an arm.

751
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:33,665
You're hopeless.

752
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:37,210
-"Raise the stakes"!
-I mean…

753
00:30:37,293 --> 00:30:40,213
I can't stand to see them take our stuff.
We have to win.

754
00:30:41,047 --> 00:30:43,258
Then, shall we raise it to 2 km?

755
00:30:43,341 --> 00:30:45,927
-No, just 1 km.
-No, let's do it like this instead.

756
00:30:46,010 --> 00:30:47,804
You all bet 1 km,

757
00:30:47,887 --> 00:30:49,556
and if you fail, we'll take 1 km.

758
00:30:49,639 --> 00:30:50,723
But we get 2 km if we win?

759
00:30:50,807 --> 00:30:52,892
If you succeed, we'll give you 2 km each.

760
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:55,645
-We should take this deal.
-Of course.

761
00:30:55,728 --> 00:30:58,648
AN INCREDIBLE OFFER

762
00:30:59,357 --> 00:31:00,859
-We'll take that deal.
-Gosh, that's…

763
00:31:01,442 --> 00:31:02,527
MAKE IT DOUBLE

764
00:31:02,610 --> 00:31:04,362
You can double the winnings. Is that okay?

765
00:31:05,071 --> 00:31:07,615
Then, let's play one more round and stop.

766
00:31:07,699 --> 00:31:09,492
-They're offering 2 km.
-Okay, let's do it.

767
00:31:09,576 --> 00:31:10,994
-Shall we play?
-Yes, let's do it.

768
00:31:11,077 --> 00:31:12,078
Chae-min will go first.

769
00:31:12,161 --> 00:31:14,289
Chae-min first.
Is the same direction okay?

770
00:31:14,372 --> 00:31:15,999
Or you can start with Dowoon,

771
00:31:16,082 --> 00:31:17,834
then go to Chae-min,
and end back at Dowoon.

772
00:31:17,917 --> 00:31:19,669
I need time to think though.

773
00:31:20,712 --> 00:31:22,672
Or should we change it? Should I go first?

774
00:31:22,755 --> 00:31:23,923
You go first.

775
00:31:24,007 --> 00:31:25,300
Yes, let's try that.

776
00:31:25,383 --> 00:31:27,635
You were like,
"Let's see how you do. You go first."

777
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:28,553
A LACK OF TRUST

778
00:31:28,636 --> 00:31:29,637
You go first.

779
00:31:30,388 --> 00:31:32,015
-Dowoon first?
-Okay.

780
00:31:32,098 --> 00:31:33,433
Okay, Dowoon will go first.

781
00:31:33,516 --> 00:31:35,685
The oldest among you is Car, the garden.

782
00:31:35,768 --> 00:31:37,478
His stage name is Car, the garden.

783
00:31:37,562 --> 00:31:39,647
Like his name,

784
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:42,650
say the name of a singer or group
with four syllables.

785
00:31:42,734 --> 00:31:44,611
Hold on a second.

786
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:46,321
Dowoon first. One, two, three.

787
00:31:46,404 --> 00:31:47,530
To More Raw.

788
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:48,656
One, two, three.

789
00:31:51,159 --> 00:31:53,578
I'll give you plenty of time.
One, two, three.

790
00:31:55,371 --> 00:31:58,166
I'm sorry,
but what's the group Dowoon is in?

791
00:31:58,249 --> 00:31:59,083
DAY6

792
00:31:59,167 --> 00:32:00,501
What group is your friend in?

793
00:32:00,585 --> 00:32:02,211
-It's DAY6!
-DAY6.

794
00:32:03,463 --> 00:32:06,758
EVEN THE DAY6 MEMBER DIDN'T KNOW

795
00:32:06,841 --> 00:32:09,093
How can we play any game with you guys?

796
00:32:09,177 --> 00:32:11,262
How do you expect to play games like this?

797
00:32:11,346 --> 00:32:12,680
Hey, he's hopeless.

798
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:13,848
-But…
-Absolutely hopeless.

799
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:15,516
Trust me, he's…

800
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:16,684
What did you come up with?

801
00:32:16,768 --> 00:32:20,021
I was thinking DAY6 and XIA Junsu.

802
00:32:20,104 --> 00:32:22,315
And I kept thinking of TVXQ.

803
00:32:23,066 --> 00:32:24,317
U-Know Yunho and XIA Junsu.

804
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:26,110
THE FOUR-SYLLABLE NICKNAME HOLDER EXCELS

805
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:30,990
-Mine was Cherry Filter.
-Cherry Filter?

806
00:32:31,074 --> 00:32:32,158
Hey, we have no chance.

807
00:32:32,241 --> 00:32:34,243
Dowoon, he can't do this.

808
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:35,912
We'll be crushed.

809
00:32:36,663 --> 00:32:38,498
To More Raw really does exist.

810
00:32:39,749 --> 00:32:41,167
-Did you guess?
-Yes.

811
00:32:41,751 --> 00:32:43,086
It really exists.

812
00:32:43,169 --> 00:32:45,046
BRIGHT, INNOCENT SMILE

813
00:32:45,838 --> 00:32:47,006
He even guessed too.

814
00:32:47,548 --> 00:32:48,716
Girls' Generation.

815
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:50,218
-Girls' Generation.
-No Brain.

816
00:32:50,301 --> 00:32:51,386
TWICE is from your agency.

817
00:32:51,469 --> 00:32:53,012
Doesn't your agency have another one?

818
00:32:53,096 --> 00:32:54,222
I'm not close with them.

819
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:57,058
What does that have to do with this?

820
00:32:57,141 --> 00:32:58,434
Good point.

821
00:32:58,518 --> 00:33:00,228
Good point. You're right.

822
00:33:00,311 --> 00:33:01,604
Are you close with To More Raw?

823
00:33:04,607 --> 00:33:06,859
Did you mention them
because you know them?

824
00:33:06,943 --> 00:33:09,779
THE WEAK LINKS ARE REVEALED
AFTER JUST TWO ROUNDS

825
00:33:09,862 --> 00:33:12,490
This was such an easy one. What a shame.

826
00:33:12,573 --> 00:33:14,450
Could you let this one slide, please?

827
00:33:14,534 --> 00:33:17,203
Just this once.
Let's give them a pass.

828
00:33:17,286 --> 00:33:19,372
Can't we have Chae-min go first?

829
00:33:19,455 --> 00:33:21,624
-I need time to think.
-Okay, Chae-min's first again.

830
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:22,709
We need time to think.

831
00:33:22,792 --> 00:33:24,836
-We're slow.
-But we have to come up with two.

832
00:33:24,919 --> 00:33:26,421
Then, let's have Tarzzan sit there.

833
00:33:26,504 --> 00:33:27,880
I'll sit over there.

834
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:30,758
I think Tarzzan
is a bit short on information.

835
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:32,218
You're right.

836
00:33:32,301 --> 00:33:33,636
TARZZAN GOES TO THE EASY SPOT

837
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:36,431
This is your last chance.
If you fail this time, we'll take 1 km.

838
00:33:36,514 --> 00:33:39,392
-But if you succeed, you get 2 km.
-We get 2 km.

839
00:33:39,475 --> 00:33:41,019
RETRY

840
00:33:41,102 --> 00:33:42,228
Chae-min will go first.

841
00:33:44,147 --> 00:33:47,525
Say a word that ends with "<i>kkang</i>."

842
00:33:47,608 --> 00:33:49,986
Chae-min will go first. One, two, three.

843
00:33:50,069 --> 00:33:51,529
-<i>Saeukkang</i> or Shrimp Crackers.
-Next.

844
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:53,239
-Roasted Pollack Crackers.
-Next.

845
00:33:53,322 --> 00:33:54,157
Damn it!

846
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:55,366
Wrong!

847
00:33:55,450 --> 00:33:56,909
What a relief! I had no idea!

848
00:33:56,993 --> 00:33:58,077
Damn it!

849
00:33:59,287 --> 00:34:00,955
What a relief! I had no idea!

850
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,415
They said all the answers already.

851
00:34:02,498 --> 00:34:03,666
HE ALSO DIDN'T HAVE ANY IDEAS

852
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:06,544
UNPRECEDENTEDLY THE WEAKEST LINK

853
00:34:06,627 --> 00:34:09,088
Geez, you guys are hopeless.

854
00:34:09,172 --> 00:34:12,383
We should teach you
a proper lesson this time.

855
00:34:12,467 --> 00:34:14,469
What? Isn't it over now?

856
00:34:14,552 --> 00:34:16,554
You asked to play games
when you're this bad?

857
00:34:17,472 --> 00:34:19,057
Hey, isn't this a difficult spot?

858
00:34:19,140 --> 00:34:20,266
But the thing is…

859
00:34:20,349 --> 00:34:22,143
I apologize. We'll do what you say.

860
00:34:22,226 --> 00:34:24,062
Because these two…

861
00:34:24,687 --> 00:34:26,522
I did have a bad feeling about them.

862
00:34:26,606 --> 00:34:29,400
But they're not really interested
in what's going on in society.

863
00:34:29,484 --> 00:34:32,153
They just go about their own lives.

864
00:34:32,236 --> 00:34:34,322
And I can clearly see that now.

865
00:34:34,405 --> 00:34:35,615
I'm sorry,

866
00:34:35,698 --> 00:34:38,409
but Car-the, please collect
the 1 km badges and give them to us.

867
00:34:39,368 --> 00:34:41,496
These two sure are smart.

868
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:44,749
Actually, it has nothing to do
with being smart.

869
00:34:45,583 --> 00:34:48,669
Chae-min, give these two a quiz.
Words that begin with something.

870
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:49,879
GLARING

871
00:34:52,507 --> 00:34:54,592
Chae-min's eyes looked so scary just now.

872
00:34:57,303 --> 00:35:00,389
HE'S VERY COMPETITIVE

873
00:35:00,473 --> 00:35:04,060
The thing is, I wanted to play games,
but Chae-min really wanted to play.

874
00:35:04,143 --> 00:35:06,938
But since it turned out like this,

875
00:35:07,814 --> 00:35:09,941
he's feeling pretty disappointed.

876
00:35:10,024 --> 00:35:11,192
He didn't expect this.

877
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:12,360
DEVASTATED EARTH ARCADE FAN

878
00:35:13,027 --> 00:35:14,612
Okay, four-character idioms.

879
00:35:14,695 --> 00:35:15,905
BLINKING

880
00:35:15,988 --> 00:35:16,989
"Four-character idioms"!

881
00:35:17,073 --> 00:35:18,825
One lap… You can just do two laps.

882
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:19,909
Okay, start!

883
00:35:19,992 --> 00:35:21,327
"The student is now the master."

884
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:23,621
"Utter chaos."

885
00:35:25,289 --> 00:35:27,208
-"Put oneself in others' shoes."
-He's good.

886
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:30,336
"Four-character idiom."

887
00:35:31,420 --> 00:35:32,964
WINNER

888
00:35:33,047 --> 00:35:35,341
You should've just said
"North, South, East, West."

889
00:35:35,424 --> 00:35:36,801
Or "A, B, C, D."

890
00:35:36,884 --> 00:35:39,262
We really don't do this.

891
00:35:39,345 --> 00:35:40,513
But we'll make it 3 km.

892
00:35:40,596 --> 00:35:41,514
Hey, this is…

893
00:35:41,597 --> 00:35:43,683
You can just bet 1 km each.

894
00:35:43,766 --> 00:35:45,476
Won't this just lead to more disaster?

895
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:46,894
-We're being suckered.
-Or…

896
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:49,480
Or we can do this. If you bet 2 km,

897
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:51,023
you could win 6 km.

898
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:54,110
A MORE SENSATIONAL OFFER

899
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:57,363
It's high return, but high risk.

900
00:35:57,446 --> 00:35:59,824
But with such risk factors that we have…

901
00:35:59,907 --> 00:36:01,534
RISK FACTOR 1, RISK FACTOR 2

902
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:03,578
If we succeed just once, we break even.

903
00:36:03,661 --> 00:36:04,745
One for three is better.

904
00:36:04,829 --> 00:36:05,913
One for three?

905
00:36:06,998 --> 00:36:08,708
If you win 3 km, you almost break even.

906
00:36:08,791 --> 00:36:10,543
We can recover our losses
and end the game.

907
00:36:10,626 --> 00:36:13,713
-Let's do this one and then decide.
-Okay.

908
00:36:13,796 --> 00:36:15,798
But even if we lose again,

909
00:36:16,632 --> 00:36:18,509
we can just bet double again, right?

910
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:21,053
GAMBLING ADDICTION WARNING

911
00:36:21,137 --> 00:36:23,139
Hey! But you know what?

912
00:36:23,222 --> 00:36:25,766
If we keep going as he just said,

913
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:27,643
and if we lose everything,

914
00:36:27,727 --> 00:36:29,687
we should use it
as a public awareness campaign.

915
00:36:30,897 --> 00:36:33,900
Instead of showing people
trembling with greed,

916
00:36:33,983 --> 00:36:37,361
just show him saying,
"Hey, we can just win it all back!"

917
00:36:38,487 --> 00:36:39,488
Then, show him

918
00:36:40,281 --> 00:36:42,116
losing everything and going hiking.

919
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:43,075
A HIKING END

920
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:45,620
WHY DO WE GAMBLE?

921
00:36:45,703 --> 00:36:47,246
They had it all planned out.

922
00:36:47,330 --> 00:36:49,040
Use it as a public service announcement.

923
00:36:49,123 --> 00:36:50,750
I just want to recover our losses.

924
00:36:50,833 --> 00:36:52,460
SINCE THEY'RE MUCH WORSE THAN EXPECTED…

925
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:54,629
Maybe we should do "Finish the Phrase."

926
00:36:54,712 --> 00:36:55,838
For example,

927
00:36:55,922 --> 00:36:57,632
-North, South…
-East, West.

928
00:36:57,715 --> 00:36:59,550
-Yes, that's it.
-Right, this game.

929
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:00,801
CHANGING THE GAME

930
00:37:00,885 --> 00:37:02,637
This game's a bit of a…

931
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:05,306
-A solo competition.
-I think we'll fail right away.

932
00:37:05,389 --> 00:37:08,142
Our show, <i>Take a Hike!</i>,

933
00:37:08,226 --> 00:37:09,727
will be streamed where?

934
00:37:09,810 --> 00:37:11,395
-Netflix.
-Yes, Netflix.

935
00:37:11,479 --> 00:37:16,108
This game will be about movie, drama,
and variety show titles on Netflix.

936
00:37:16,192 --> 00:37:17,443
I like that.

937
00:37:17,526 --> 00:37:18,819
Chae-min will go first.

938
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:20,988
HIS FACE CONTORTS IN AGONY

939
00:37:21,072 --> 00:37:23,241
HIS FACE CONTORTS TOO

940
00:37:23,324 --> 00:37:24,867
Hold on. Hey!

941
00:37:24,951 --> 00:37:26,702
They can't do this!

942
00:37:26,786 --> 00:37:28,287
WILL THEY DO BETTER?

943
00:37:28,371 --> 00:37:29,372
But Dowoon is also…

944
00:37:32,041 --> 00:37:34,252
Chae-min will go first. Here we go.

945
00:37:34,877 --> 00:37:36,254
-Single's…
-Inferno!

946
00:37:36,879 --> 00:37:38,089
All of Us…

947
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:40,299
-Are Dead.
-Correct.

948
00:37:40,383 --> 00:37:41,300
Stranger…

949
00:37:42,218 --> 00:37:43,177
Who's that?

950
00:37:43,261 --> 00:37:45,763
No! I'll answer it instead!

951
00:37:45,846 --> 00:37:46,847
Stranger…

952
00:37:47,848 --> 00:37:49,141
-Who's that?
-No!

953
00:37:49,225 --> 00:37:51,352
HE TURNS INTO A TYRANT

954
00:37:52,019 --> 00:37:52,853
Who's that?

955
00:37:52,937 --> 00:37:55,481
No! I'll answer it instead!

956
00:37:56,315 --> 00:37:58,276
CHAOS

957
00:37:58,359 --> 00:38:00,152
Can I answer it instead? Just this once.

958
00:38:01,696 --> 00:38:02,822
Can you believe this?

959
00:38:02,905 --> 00:38:04,407
"Stranger Who's That?"

960
00:38:05,199 --> 00:38:08,953
I'll answer the "Stranger" one.

961
00:38:09,036 --> 00:38:09,996
-Stranger…
-Things.

962
00:38:10,079 --> 00:38:12,957
Wait, I heard it as the name "Kim Ui-han."

963
00:38:13,624 --> 00:38:15,668
-So… Hold on. Seriously.
-Right!

964
00:38:15,751 --> 00:38:18,254
Wait, I heard it as the name "Kim Ui-han."

965
00:38:19,088 --> 00:38:20,423
FEELING WRONGED

966
00:38:20,506 --> 00:38:22,633
-Seriously.
-That's why he was flustered!

967
00:38:22,717 --> 00:38:24,135
That's why he asked, "Who's that?"

968
00:38:24,218 --> 00:38:26,804
Seriously, I'm not exaggerating.

969
00:38:26,887 --> 00:38:29,390
That's why I asked, "Who's that?"

970
00:38:30,016 --> 00:38:31,767
BURSTING INTO LAUGHTER

971
00:38:32,560 --> 00:38:34,562
Of course, he'd get flustered.

972
00:38:34,645 --> 00:38:35,896
The finger!

973
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:37,315
The finger fell off!

974
00:38:37,398 --> 00:38:39,900
Come on, that's ridiculous!

975
00:38:39,984 --> 00:38:42,403
Of course, if I heard "Stranger,"
I would've said "Things."

976
00:38:42,486 --> 00:38:43,529
No way!

977
00:38:43,612 --> 00:38:44,947
Who's Kim Ui-han?

978
00:38:45,031 --> 00:38:47,408
-You can check the footage.
-No way!

979
00:38:47,491 --> 00:38:50,286
I mean, you heard me ask, "Who's that?"

980
00:38:50,369 --> 00:38:51,871
-Yes, he asked, "Who's that?"
-Yeah.

981
00:38:51,954 --> 00:38:54,457
If I heard "Stranger,"
I wouldn't say, "Who's that?"

982
00:38:54,540 --> 00:38:56,167
-Are Dead.
-Correct.

983
00:38:56,250 --> 00:38:57,168
Stranger…

984
00:38:58,169 --> 00:38:59,003
Who's that?

985
00:38:59,086 --> 00:39:00,588
No! I'll answer it instead!

986
00:39:00,671 --> 00:39:03,341
ISN'T FEELING WRONGED AT ALL

987
00:39:03,424 --> 00:39:06,594
If he thought he heard a name,
he obviously would be confused.

988
00:39:06,677 --> 00:39:08,346
-Yeah.
-He suddenly heard a name.

989
00:39:08,429 --> 00:39:11,390
If it were me,
I would've reacted the same way.

990
00:39:11,474 --> 00:39:14,101
If I heard "Stranger,"
I would've said "Things" for sure.

991
00:39:14,852 --> 00:39:15,686
Seriously?

992
00:39:15,770 --> 00:39:18,898
I even downloaded
some episodes of <i>Stranger Things.</i>

993
00:39:18,981 --> 00:39:20,608
If you really did, I'll let it slide.

994
