These are so easy.

1245
00:48:15,225 --> 00:48:16,560
"LMO."

1246
00:48:16,643 --> 00:48:18,645
-"Looks make the outfit."
-Correct.

1247
00:48:19,605 --> 00:48:20,856
"OAL."

1248
00:48:21,481 --> 00:48:22,774
"Obviously sturdy…"

1249
00:48:22,858 --> 00:48:24,067
What was that?

1250
00:48:24,151 --> 00:48:25,235
-"OA…"
-What?

1251
00:48:25,319 --> 00:48:26,570
"Obviously sturdy

1252
00:48:26,653 --> 00:48:28,280
and lasting human wall."

1253
00:48:28,363 --> 00:48:30,157
APPLAUDING

1254
00:48:30,240 --> 00:48:31,617
Hey, that's correct!

1255
00:48:31,700 --> 00:48:32,534
DUMBFOUNDED

1256
00:48:32,618 --> 00:48:33,994
So you knew!

1257
00:48:34,077 --> 00:48:35,162
How did you know?

1258
00:48:35,245 --> 00:48:36,330
-Really?
-Wrong!

1259
00:48:37,831 --> 00:48:39,916
"Obviously high
and lasting wall of humans"?

1260
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:41,752
"Obviously sturdy
and lasting human wall."

1261
00:48:43,253 --> 00:48:45,339
-Go through the words again.
-"Human wall."

1262
00:48:45,422 --> 00:48:47,215
"Gosh, Car-the is OAL."

1263
00:48:47,299 --> 00:48:48,508
Yeah, OAL.

1264
00:48:49,343 --> 00:48:51,219
I guess we gave him one that was too hard.

1265
00:48:51,303 --> 00:48:53,305
Yes, OAL is too difficult.

1266
00:48:53,388 --> 00:48:56,642
But for others, OAL isn't that…

1267
00:48:56,725 --> 00:48:58,852
-Not hard at all, right?
-It's not hard.

1268
00:48:58,935 --> 00:49:01,104
Wait, so what's OAL?

1269
00:49:01,188 --> 00:49:03,065
-What does it mean?
-"Another level."

1270
00:49:03,148 --> 00:49:05,025
It stands for "another level"?

1271
00:49:05,108 --> 00:49:05,984
Yeah.

1272
00:49:06,735 --> 00:49:09,029
OAL means "another level"?

1273
00:49:09,112 --> 00:49:11,698
LMO means "looks make the outfit."

1274
00:49:11,782 --> 00:49:12,783
But OAL means…

1275
00:49:12,866 --> 00:49:13,950
"On."

1276
00:49:14,034 --> 00:49:15,410
Oh, "on a level"?

1277
00:49:15,494 --> 00:49:16,620
"Another level."

1278
00:49:17,245 --> 00:49:21,083
So, OAL stands for "on another…"

1279
00:49:21,166 --> 00:49:22,793
Who are you fighting with?

1280
00:49:23,627 --> 00:49:27,047
It looks like he's fighting
with his own self.

1281
00:49:27,631 --> 00:49:29,216
He's trying to make himself understand.

1282
00:49:29,299 --> 00:49:30,759
He's arguing with himself.

1283
00:49:30,842 --> 00:49:31,885
Wait, look.

1284
00:49:31,968 --> 00:49:34,596
-DCC is "Dubai chewy cookie."
-Yes.

1285
00:49:34,680 --> 00:49:37,099
OAL is "another level"?

1286
00:49:37,182 --> 00:49:39,726
It starts with… "on."

1287
00:49:39,810 --> 00:49:41,478
-"Another level."
-"On."

1288
00:49:41,561 --> 00:49:43,271
He really is something.

1289
00:49:43,355 --> 00:49:44,481
HE FINALLY UNDERSTANDS IT

1290
00:49:44,564 --> 00:49:46,149
"On another level."

1291
00:49:46,233 --> 00:49:47,901
People like you are "on another level."

1292
00:49:47,984 --> 00:49:50,445
"On another level." I see.

1293
00:49:51,029 --> 00:49:53,740
Man, if you had never learned
how to play the drums…

1294
00:49:54,658 --> 00:49:56,785
-You'd be struggling too.
-Okay, I got it now.

1295
00:49:56,868 --> 00:49:59,162
BORN TO BE A DRUMMER

1296
00:49:59,246 --> 00:50:02,290
If you each get two questions right,
we'll let things slide.

1297
00:50:02,374 --> 00:50:03,500
-It's for them.
-Good luck.

1298
00:50:03,583 --> 00:50:05,293
"IAEIF."

1299
00:50:05,377 --> 00:50:06,878
"Iced Americano even if freezing."

1300
00:50:06,962 --> 00:50:09,131
-Okay!
-That was great.

1301
00:50:09,214 --> 00:50:10,507
It's looking good.

1302
00:50:10,590 --> 00:50:11,800
"SELP."

1303
00:50:14,761 --> 00:50:16,680
Three, two…

1304
00:50:16,763 --> 00:50:19,516
"Scrounge everything and pull…" Damn.

1305
00:50:19,599 --> 00:50:21,768
It's right, isn't it? It was similar.

1306
00:50:21,852 --> 00:50:23,145
"Scrape every last penny"!

1307
00:50:23,228 --> 00:50:24,980
Yes, that's right! Correct!

1308
00:50:25,063 --> 00:50:26,857
-"Every last penny"!
-Yes, that's right!

1309
00:50:26,940 --> 00:50:28,567
Correct!

1310
00:50:29,234 --> 00:50:31,361
They counted it as correct!

1311
00:50:31,445 --> 00:50:33,822
You don't have to put a time limit.

1312
00:50:33,905 --> 00:50:35,073
DODGED A BULLET

1313
00:50:35,157 --> 00:50:36,658
"SNC."

1314
00:50:37,492 --> 00:50:39,369
"Seeking a natural connection"!

1315
00:50:39,453 --> 00:50:41,121
Yes!

1316
00:50:42,456 --> 00:50:44,040
Here comes the last one.

1317
00:50:45,041 --> 00:50:46,626
NIS.

1318
00:50:46,710 --> 00:50:47,669
What?

1319
00:50:48,420 --> 00:50:49,963
NIS.

1320
00:50:50,046 --> 00:50:51,339
What?

1321
00:50:51,423 --> 00:50:52,674
NIS.

1322
00:50:53,467 --> 00:50:55,844
You know this. Think carefully.

1323
00:50:55,927 --> 00:50:57,137
National Intelligence Service!

1324
00:50:57,220 --> 00:50:58,430
-Yes!
-Yes!

1325
00:50:58,513 --> 00:50:59,723
National Intelligence Service!

1326
00:50:59,806 --> 00:51:01,057
-Yes!
-Yes!

1327
00:51:02,809 --> 00:51:04,311
-Chae-min.
-Yes?

1328
00:51:05,562 --> 00:51:08,815
People all around Asia
will be watching this.

1329
00:51:08,899 --> 00:51:12,194
-I don't know anything about that.
-Many children will be watching.

1330
00:51:12,277 --> 00:51:16,281
It's important to show
we're honest and trustworthy.

1331
00:51:16,364 --> 00:51:19,743
While walking by him just now,
did you, by any chance,

1332
00:51:19,826 --> 00:51:20,827
though I doubt it,

1333
00:51:21,453 --> 00:51:23,663
tell him the answer?

1334
00:51:23,747 --> 00:51:25,749
If you say no, we'll have to believe you.

1335
00:51:25,832 --> 00:51:27,083
Chae-min's not like that.

1336
00:51:27,167 --> 00:51:29,419
Did you tell him or not?

1337
00:51:29,503 --> 00:51:30,712
Did I tell you or not?

1338
00:51:30,796 --> 00:51:31,880
Did he tell me or not?

1339
00:51:34,633 --> 00:51:36,051
-Yes or no?
-I didn't hear anything.

1340
00:51:36,134 --> 00:51:38,053
He said he didn't hear anything.

1341
00:51:38,720 --> 00:51:40,096
I just thought,

1342
00:51:40,180 --> 00:51:43,058
"Gosh, I knew Dowoon could do it."

1343
00:51:43,141 --> 00:51:45,644
I mean, he could've just said your name.

1344
00:51:45,727 --> 00:51:47,813
-Your name is Jung-won.
-Yeah, it sounds similar.

1345
00:51:47,896 --> 00:51:49,397
-Car, the Jung-won.
-Yeah.

1346
00:51:50,023 --> 00:51:51,858
-Car, the Jung-won!
-Car, the Jung-won!

1347
00:51:51,942 --> 00:51:53,318
National Intelligence Service!

1348
00:51:55,237 --> 00:51:56,947
You knew the answer, right?

1349
00:51:57,030 --> 00:51:58,782
Of course, he did.
How could he not know it?

1350
00:51:58,865 --> 00:52:00,659
Every Korean should know this.

1351
00:52:00,742 --> 00:52:02,244
See? He says he knew.

1352
00:52:02,327 --> 00:52:04,120
You knew about the NIS, right?

1353
00:52:04,204 --> 00:52:05,330
Of course.

1354
00:52:05,413 --> 00:52:07,290
-You knew?
-Of course.

1355
00:52:07,374 --> 00:52:09,668
I'll have our sound mixer check the facts.

1356
00:52:09,751 --> 00:52:12,629
But if our sound mixer
checks the sound levels later

1357
00:52:12,712 --> 00:52:15,882
and notices Chae-min's lips and voice

1358
00:52:15,966 --> 00:52:17,676
saying "National Intelligence Service,"

1359
00:52:17,759 --> 00:52:21,096
then to all the young fans around Asia

1360
00:52:21,179 --> 00:52:22,597
who expected honesty…

1361
00:52:22,681 --> 00:52:25,058
Then, you'd truly be a tyrant.

1362
00:52:27,018 --> 00:52:28,895
-You have to just push ahead.
-Simply a tyrant.

1363
00:52:28,979 --> 00:52:31,064
"He's a real tyrant like his character."

1364
00:52:31,147 --> 00:52:32,732
"Oh, that tyrant?"

1365
00:52:35,777 --> 00:52:37,320
I told him the answer.

1366
00:52:39,406 --> 00:52:43,201
HE COMES CLEAN

1367
00:52:44,786 --> 00:52:46,413
-Chae-min is…
-Bring us the 5 km badges.

1368
00:52:46,496 --> 00:52:48,373
Give us the 5 km badges.

1369
00:52:48,957 --> 00:52:52,127
Chae-min chose honesty in the end.

1370
00:52:52,210 --> 00:52:54,129
In various interviews,

1371
00:52:54,212 --> 00:52:57,507
I said my strength is honesty, so…

1372
00:52:58,592 --> 00:53:01,720
I couldn't bring myself to keep lying.

1373
00:53:03,138 --> 00:53:05,891
You may get another chance
to win these kilometers back.

1374
00:53:05,974 --> 00:53:07,934
I'm sure you'll get the chance.

1375
00:53:08,018 --> 00:53:11,021
It might get hard on you
if we keep going, so shall we wrap up?

1376
00:53:11,104 --> 00:53:12,105
THEY END LOSING 5 KM EACH

1377
00:53:13,064 --> 00:53:15,901
But regardless of the result
of these games,

1378
00:53:15,984 --> 00:53:18,570
I can't think of any way to win them back.

1379
00:53:18,653 --> 00:53:19,613
Exactly.

1380
00:53:20,697 --> 00:53:22,908
Getting angry and stealing them

1381
00:53:23,783 --> 00:53:25,994
or taking them by force are the only ways.

1382
00:53:27,037 --> 00:53:28,705
THE NEXT DAY

1383
00:53:30,582 --> 00:53:31,416
Let's go.

1384
00:53:32,959 --> 00:53:34,127
Come over here.

1385
00:53:34,210 --> 00:53:35,545
WHILE HIKING THE YEONGNAM ALPS

1386
00:53:35,629 --> 00:53:36,463
We should head out.

1387
00:53:36,546 --> 00:53:37,964
-Let's move out.
-Let's go.

1388
00:53:38,548 --> 00:53:40,300
By the way, where's Producer Nah?

1389
00:53:40,383 --> 00:53:42,302
I think he's way behind us.

1390
00:53:42,385 --> 00:53:45,138
No, I think he took a car down
from that rest stop earlier.

1391
00:53:46,765 --> 00:53:49,643
At some point,
we didn't see him climbing up.

1392
00:53:50,977 --> 00:53:52,103
I realized he abandoned us.

1393
00:53:52,187 --> 00:53:55,899
PRODUCER NAH HAS DISAPPEARED

1394
00:53:55,982 --> 00:53:57,150
-Jung-won.
-Yeah?

1395
00:53:57,233 --> 00:53:59,194
You know Yung-suk ran off, right?

1396
00:53:59,277 --> 00:54:01,112
Yeah. When did he leave?

1397
00:54:01,196 --> 00:54:04,783
I mean, after he took
our badges like that yesterday…

1398
00:54:04,866 --> 00:54:07,202
I feel so angry all of a sudden.

1399
00:54:07,285 --> 00:54:09,412
I've never seen him
say anything like that before.

1400
00:54:10,830 --> 00:54:12,457
What did I do wrong? What is it?

1401
00:54:12,540 --> 00:54:14,125
Chae-min, why are you so angry?

1402
00:54:14,209 --> 00:54:15,710
PRODUCER NAH IS BACKED INTO A CORNER

1403
00:54:15,794 --> 00:54:17,045
Where were you earlier?

1404
00:54:18,254 --> 00:54:22,384
EVERY TIME SOMEONE STEPS AWAY

1405
00:54:23,426 --> 00:54:27,931
SECRET DEALS ARE MADE

1406
00:54:28,014 --> 00:54:30,100
-I only drink Sprite.
-Chae-min only drinks Sprite.

1407
00:54:30,183 --> 00:54:31,518
There are two cups. How strange.

1408
00:54:31,601 --> 00:54:34,688
NEW SUSPICIOUSLY CLOSE TIES

1409
00:54:36,731 --> 00:54:38,483
Congratulations on climbing
the three peaks.

1410
00:54:38,566 --> 00:54:43,405
COLLUSION DISGUISED AS RECONCILIATION

1411
00:54:47,742 --> 00:54:49,577
What a shame.
Still, let's give him a hand.

1412
00:54:49,661 --> 00:54:50,495
Why?

1413
00:54:50,578 --> 00:54:52,956
AND THE ONE LEFT OUT

1414
00:54:53,039 --> 00:54:55,917
You jerks made a deal while I was away!

1415
00:54:56,001 --> 00:54:59,045
I hurried my way down
and gave all of you rides!

1416
00:54:59,129 --> 00:54:59,963
-You little…
-Dowoon.

1417
00:55:00,046 --> 00:55:01,840
I thought highly of you!

1418
00:55:01,923 --> 00:55:03,341
Hear me out.

1419
00:56:01,399 --> 00:56:03,401
Subtitle translation by: Wayne Ryu
